# Superpowers (project)

This project uses [Superpowers](https://github.com/obra/superpowers) (vendored in `vendor/superpowers/`).

## Mandatory behavior

**Before any response or action** — including clarifying questions, codebase exploration, or file reads — check whether a Superpowers skill applies. If it might apply (even 1%), read and follow it.

1. Read `.cursor/skills/using-superpowers/SKILL.md` at session start (also injected by the `sessionStart` hook when available).
2. For Cursor-specific tool mapping, read `.cursor/skills/using-superpowers/references/cursor-tools.md`.
3. When a skill applies, announce "Using [skill] to [purpose]" and follow the skill exactly.

## Skill locations

| Location | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `.cursor/skills/` | Active skills for Cursor / cloud agent discovery |
| `vendor/superpowers/skills/` | Upstream source (update with `scripts/update-superpowers.ps1`) |

## Common triggers

| Situation | Skill |
| --- | --- |
| New feature, component, or behavior change | `brainstorming` |
| Bug, test failure, unexpected behavior | `systematic-debugging` |
| Approved design → implementation plan | `writing-plans` |
| Plan ready → execute | `subagent-driven-development` or `executing-plans` |
| Writing code | `test-driven-development` |
| Claiming work is done | `verification-before-completion` |

Full skill index: `.cursor/CLOUD.md`

User instructions in `AGENTS.md` and explicit user requests override skill workflows.
